  "question": {
    "text": "Pick out the incorrect statement.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Wato2",
      "text": "The geometry around 'N' atom in trimethylamine is pyramidal",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "P6YnR",
      "text": "The geometry around N atom in trisilylamine is planar",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8yN7v",
      "text": "The nitrogen atom in trimethylamine is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> -hybridized; whilst in trisilylamine it is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> -hybridized",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sjqBn",
      "text": "Trisilylamine has donor properties; whilst trimethylamine has no donor properties",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In trimethylamine, 'N' atom is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> -hybridized. <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/dc1c7b61-4e17-4070-858e-e8913edc4d31.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:4.59167in;height:1.45833in\"> <br/>Due to the presence of lone pair in <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> -hybrid orbital, the geometry of <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> becomes pyramidal around nitrogen. <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/4e480a17-026b-45ea-8bc9-c4d787c06aee.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.78333in;height:1.4in\"> <br/>This lone pair of electrons can be donated to electron-deficient species, e.g., <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> . This lone pair cannot be transferred to carbon atom, because carbon atom has no d-orbital in its valence shell. <br/>In <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the 'N' atom is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> -hybridized. <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/217bbe5c-43a0-4a2f-b9c1-11f067f8358a.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:4.50833in;height:0.81667in\"> <br/>The orientation of three <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> -hybrid orbitals is plane-triangular, therefore, the geometry around 'N' becomes plane-triangular. Here the lone pair of electrons is transferred to vacant d-orbitals to each of three silicon atoms forming <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> multiple bonds. Consequently, <math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> has no donor properties. For example <br/><math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo></math> No reaction. <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/7cafa8a2-56b2-4db4-a721-ac38231f1d49.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.85833in;height:1.50833in\">",
    "image": null
  },
